These Alloy files are versions of view-backing.als from the expert models corpus which have transformations
done on them to remove the sig hierarchy. This also includes splitting out function arguments into each having
one sig, etc. These transformations are intended to be done automatically by the preprocessor in the future,
but are included here for experimentation before the full preprocessor is implemented.

Still to be done as of view-backing-transformed-2-v2.als:
- split out let variables into one per sig, like with function arguments
- fix constraints for split fields: "f: A -> one (B+C)" should not be split into "f_B: A -> one B"
  and "f_C: A -> one C" and blindly combined as "f_B + f_C" whenever f is mentioned, because that
  results in expressions violating the original "one" constraint. Instead there should be some combination
  of "lone" and extra constraints.
